in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @magic
in @frame
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/surface — the Surface Model species. First sub-prism of the
# @smarts substrate-architectural integration: language → query at the
# four-Models pipeline (Surface → Mirror → Shatter → Reflection).
#
# Tick 63 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 62's residue: @smarts
# cross-family adapter set closed (6/6). With the adapters in place,
# the four Models can be substrate-decl'd; each Model composes the
# integration discipline at its altitude.
#
# Per shards/smarts.mirror #83 + reference-mirror-spectral-spec
# (commit a8055f0):
#
#   - Surface translates: language → query        (Explorer model)
#   - Mirror navigates:   query → graph path      (Fate model)
#   - Shatter renders:    graph path → text       (Cartographer model)
#   - Reflection observes: pipeline → adjustments (Abyss model)
#
# This shard lands the FIRST Model (Surface). Three more remain to
# complete the @smarts Model set; reflection landed at an earlier
# tick.
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# The Surface Model IS the substrate's translation primitive at
# language-to-query altitude. A reader speaks in natural-language;
# Surface translates into a graph-query shape the Mirror Model can
# navigate. The substrate-pull-correct shape: typed language
# carrier, typed query carrier, bilateral predicate that discharges
# translation-grounds-query.
#
# At the integration altitude: Surface operates WITHIN the @smarts
# integration discipline (discipline_flexible holds throughout
# translation). The translation is bounded under perturbation per the
# @smarts integration's discipline-flexibility requirement.
#
# === The four Models compose the substrate's pipeline ===
#
# The Surface Model's translation IS the first step of the substrate's
# query-answering pipeline. The Mirror Model navigates the query;
# the Shatter Model renders the navigated graph; the Reflection Model
# observes the whole pipeline and adjusts. Surface is the entry
# point; without Surface, no language enters the substrate's
# graph-altitude reasoning.
#
# Per [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]] +
# reference-mirror-spectral-spec: Reflection composes with Surface
# at the pipeline boundary; Reflection's adjustments tune Surface's
# translation patterns based on observed reader engagement. The
# substrate-pull-correct loop: Surface translates; pipeline runs;
# Reflection observes; Reflection adjusts Surface's weights for next
# tick.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `language` carrier: typed reference for the natural-language
#   input artifact (a string, a span, a sentence — substrate-decl'd
#   as ref because the language vocabulary is parametric).
# - `query` carrier: typed reference for the graph-query output
#   artifact (a Prism composition, a graph navigation specification
#   — substrate-decl'd as ref because the query vocabulary is
#   parametric).
# - `surface_result` carrier: typed record (language, query, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural output of a translation operation.
# - `translate` action: the load-bearing action at @smarts/surface
#   altitude. Takes language + the @smarts integration + perturbation;
#   returns surface_result; requires discipline_flexible (the
#   @smarts integration must maintain discipline-flexibility for
#   translation to be admissible).
# - `translation_grounds_query` predicate: bilateral verdict that the
#   surface_result's query IS grounded in the language (preserves
#   substrate-architectural meaning across translation).
# - `refine` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   translation-refinement discipline (the Surface-altitude
#   operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes a
#   query + a sound surface_result + perturbation; returns the
#   refined query.
#
# === The translation-grounds-query discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 + the substrate-pull discipline: when Surface
# translates, the substrate's query-vocabulary tightens. The
# substrate-decl content is unchanged; the translation acquires
# sharper alignment with the substrate's graph-altitude vocabulary.
# The natural-language was approximate; the query is structure-
# preserving.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at translation-altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Surface (honest): translates by preserving substrate-
# architectural meaning; admits when the natural-language ambiguity
# forced a translation choice; surfaces alternative queries when
# multiple substrate-pull-correct interpretations exist.
#
# Narcissus-pole Surface (deceptive): imposes one query interpretation
# without admitting alternatives; uses translation framing to obscure
# substrate-architectural ambiguity; the query carries author-framing
# rather than language-meaning.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole translation at substrate altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   compiler frontends          Aho-Lam-Sethi-Ullman 1986 (Dragon
#                               Book). The canonical structural
#                               ancestor of language → IR translation.
#   semantic parsing            Zettlemoyer-Collins 2005. The
#                               substrate-decl ancestor of language →
#                               graph-query translation.
#   knowledge representation    Brachman-Levesque 2004. The substrate
#                               ancestor of graph-altitude query
#                               structures.
#   natural language statistical Manning-Schütze 1999. The cultural-
#                               practice ancestor of probabilistic
#                               translation patterns.
#   query languages             Codd 1970 (relational model). The
#                               substrate-altitude ancestor of
#                               structured query forms.
#   information retrieval       Salton 1971. The substrate-decl
#                               ancestor of language-grounded
#                               relevance ranking.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root; declares
#               this species as one of four sub-prisms);
#               reference-mirror-spectral-spec (commit a8055f0; the
#               four-Models architecture canonical doc).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-reflection-thinks-in-spectral-questions]]
#                       (the Reflection Model composes with Surface at
#                       the pipeline boundary),
#                      [[reference-mirror-spectral-spec]]
#                       (the four-Models architecture spec),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: smarts.mirror (the family-root; declares
#                  discipline_flexible this species first-consumes),
#                 smarts/reflection.mirror (the fourth Model;
#                  Reflection observes Surface's translation patterns
#                  and adjusts via the pipeline boundary),
#                 smarts/mirror.mirror (the second Model; consumes
#                  Surface's query output; forward-promised),
#                 smarts/shatter.mirror (the third Model; renders the
#                  graph path; forward-promised),
#                 smarts/{magic, pack, frame, cyberpunk,
#                 epistemologic, kintsugi}.mirror (the cross-family
#                 adapters; Surface composes with each integration
#                 family at the @smarts altitude).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/surface.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/surface` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/compilers/aho-1986
source @arxiv/nlp/zettlemoyer-collins-2005
source @arxiv/ai/brachman-levesque-2004
source @arxiv/nlp/manning-schutze-1999
source @arxiv/databases/codd-1970
source @arxiv/information-retrieval/salton-1971

prism @smarts/surface {
  focus surface
  project surface
  split surface
  shift surface
  settle surface
}

# === The language carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for natural-language input. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref. The
# substrate-input of the Surface Model. Forward-promised refinement:
# typed record (text, span, tokens, language_id) at species-or-
# extension altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type language = ref

# === The query carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference for the graph-query output. Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref. The
# substrate-output of the Surface Model, consumed by the Mirror
# Model. Forward-promised refinement: typed record (prism_composition,
# operation_sequence, navigation_target) at species-or-extension
# altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type query = ref

# === The surface_result carrier ===
#
# Per the @smarts/<species> template + Surface's typed-record
# discipline: typed record over (language, query, verdict). The
# substrate-architectural output of a translation operation. Carries:
#
# - lang : the input language artifact
# - q    : the output query Surface produced
# - v    : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → query GROUNDED in language;
#          DEFENSIVE → translation requires substrate-pull revision)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type surface_result = {
  lang: language,
  q:    query,
  v:    verdict,
}

# === translate action (FIRST consumer of discipline_flexible) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @smarts/surface altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for language → query translation at the
# @smarts integration altitude. Realizes Surface's translation
# discipline as substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a language artifact (natural-language input), the @smarts
# integration the translation operates within, and the perturbation
# under which the translation is checked; returns a typed
# surface_result carrying the query and verdict.
#
# requires discipline_flexible(s, p): the @smarts integration must
# maintain substrate-architectural discipline-flexibility under
# perturbation BEFORE the translation is admissible. This is the
# @smarts-altitude first-consumer pattern (same shape as the
# @pack/<peer> species's requires pack_coherent).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual translation
# primitive is implemented by Surface's Explorer-Model frame at
# runtime altitude (forward-promised: weights, biases, fulfilled
# receipts per .shatter v1 per reflection-model spec).
translate(lang: language, s: smarts, p: perturbation) -> surface_result
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
{ \ }

# === translation_grounds_query predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# translation discipline. Consumer shards (refine, below;
# forward-promised Mirror Model consuming the query) name `requires
# translation_grounds_query(sr, p)` to declare bilateral agreement
# that the surface_result's query IS grounded in the language.
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct language-grounding check at the
# species boundary. Composes with @smarts's discipline_flexible at
# the integration altitude.
#
# Bounded → query grounded in language meaning (Splinter-pole case);
# unbounded → query imposes translation framing without language
# ground (Narcissus-pole case; alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57
# distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @smarts cross-family
# adapters carry (smarts_satisfies_<family>), @pack carries
# (pack_coherent), @magic carries (invariant_preserved, audited).
translation_grounds_query(sr: surface_result, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === refine action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the translation-refinement
# discipline at @smarts/surface altitude (the Surface-altitude
# operational form of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes a
# query + a sound surface_result + the perturbation under which
# soundness was checked; returns the refined query.
#
# Per recognition #57: refine operates at the @io boundary. The
# query becomes a refined query preserved under translation-grounding.
# The substrate's capability is unchanged; the query's language-
# ground tightens.
#
# requires translation_grounds_query(sr, p): the substrate forecloses
# refinement from an ungrounded translation. Narcissus-pole queries
# (framing-imposition without language ground) cannot drive query-
# refinement. The bilateral predicate IS the boundary-harness.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual query-
# refinement transformation is the substrate's translation-grounds-
# query loop.
refine(q: query, sr: surface_result, p: perturbation) -> query
requires translation_grounds_query(sr, p)
{ \ }

out @smarts/surface
out language
out query
out surface_result
out translate
out translation_grounds_query
out refine
